conforms to · Risk: high · ∥: yes

==================================================================================================
0. HOW TO READ THIS FILE
==================================================================================================

NOTATION   This file reuses the local declarative notation Artifact 067 chose for its own
           contract. It is an implementation choice, not COOLBOY12 architecture, and establishes
           no repository-wide schema language (SC-069-B). No parser exists for it.

           ELEMENT <name>        a structural element of a materialized Record
           LAYER                 ENVELOPE (universal, RMS §4) or FAMILY (Registry-model-owned)
           REQUIRED              yes | no
           CARDINALITY           exactly-one | …
           CONSTRAINT            what a conforming value must satisfy
           CHECK                 how the constraint is checked — the one addition to 067's
                                 notation, a 069 choice:
                                   NATIVE    decidable from the Record alone
                                   EXTERNAL  needs evidence outside the Record; the line names
                                             who supplies it, and this contract does not claim
                                             it proven
                                   STATIC    a property of this contract, checked by reading it
           BASIS                 SOURCE FACT · REQUIRED SYNTHESIS · 069 CHOICE, with its source
           REJECT                a value that does not conform

STATUS     This contract describes the structure a materialized KIND-DEFINITION Record must
           satisfy. It is not a KIND-DEFINITION Record, not a SCHEMA-DEFINITION Record, not the
           schema of any defined Kind's Records, and not canonical data. It is an authored source
           outside canon/** (Roadmap §0.8; CONFLICT-F). Concrete KIND-DEFINITION Records are
           committed only through the Mutation Coordinator (row 152) after G-CANON-R. Where this
           contract differs from the Master Blueprint, the Record Model System, the Roadmap, or
           Artifact 068, those sources are right and this contract is wrong.

SPEC       Artifact 068 — docs/registry/kind_definition.md — is the semantic contract this file
           encodes, consumed unchanged (H: 068). This file encodes only the structural
           consequences of the obligations 068 establishes (068 §21). Artifact 067 is a precedent
           for notation only; nothing here is derived from the MODEL-DEFINITION family.

==================================================================================================
1. RECORD SHAPE
==================================================================================================

KIND-DEFINITION RECORD
├── ENVELOPE  partition · kind · object_id · slug · provenance · registry_ref · sot_class
└── FAMILY    subject_model · subject_kind · definition
              └── subject_model and subject_kind together carry the ONE semantic subject

Artifact 069 defines exactly these ten elements: the universal seven-field envelope (RMS §4) and
three family elements. It defines no other element.

That is the scope boundary of this contract, not a closure over everything a KIND-DEFINITION
Record may later carry. Rows 108–110 keep their authority to establish Registry-owned evolution,
versioning, supersession and deprecation representation (§5 VERSIONABILITY). The envelope, by
contrast, stays exactly seven fields: no downstream Registry representation becomes an eighth
universal field (RMS §4; P-05).

One subject, two carriers. 068 requires exactly one declared Kind of exactly one owning Record
Model as the semantic subject, and fixes no count of structural carriers (068 RF-068-1, RF-068-4).
This contract carries that one subject in two elements: subject_model gives the owning model's
scope and subject_kind names the Kind within it. Neither element alone is a subject; together they
are exactly one.

Two meanings of "kind", never merged. The envelope element kind names this Record's own Kind —
always KIND-DEFINITION. The family element subject_kind names the declared Kind this Record
defines — for example CHARACTER. They are different elements in different roles. Their values
coincide only in the one KIND-DEFINITION whose subject is the Kind KIND-DEFINITION itself (§6).

==================================================================================================
2. ENVELOPE — the universal seven (RMS §4; Artifact 033)
==================================================================================================

Types, defaults, nullability and serialization of the envelope fields are not established by the
governing sources (Artifact 033) and are not stated here.

ELEMENT     partition
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  R — the Registry partition
CHECK       NATIVE
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — a KIND-DEFINITION is a Registry Record (RMS §10, §10.1; 068 §5)

ELEMENT     kind
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  identifies the declared Registry Kind KIND-DEFINITION (Kind 2 of RMS §10.1) — this
            Record's own Kind, never its subject. The constraint is symbolic. No two-character
            Registry Kind code is established; none is minted here (SC-069-C).
CHECK       NATIVE against the symbolic Kind; against a code only once the Registry's codes are
            bound by their own rows (row 117; Artifact 060 writes the code schematically as <kind>)
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §10.1; Artifact 064 §9
REJECT      any other Registry Kind; the subject Kind (for example CHARACTER) placed here; any
            invented code (for example KD) presented as established

ELEMENT     object_id
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the object identity component under the universal identity grammar. It is this
            Record's identity — neither the defined Kind nor the Kind's code (068 RS-068-1).
CHECK       NATIVE
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4, §5; 068 RS-068-1

ELEMENT     slug
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  decoration only; never identity, never the basis of resolution
CHECK       NATIVE
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §5; Artifact 033

ELEMENT     provenance
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it; provenance meaning is not defined here
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033

ELEMENT     registry_ref
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the universal envelope field, unchanged. This contract attaches no referent,
            self-reference convention, bootstrap target or resolution meaning to it, and it does
            not carry the subject.
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033 leaves its referent unresolved; Blueprint §9.4:
            reference resolution is not Registry work

ELEMENT     sot_class
LAYER       ENVELOPE
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  as the universal envelope carries it. No value is fixed here; Artifact 069's own
            manifest SoT and Canon are not Record-level values and are not copied into it.
CHECK       NATIVE for presence
BASIS       SOURCE FACT — RMS §4; Artifact 033

==================================================================================================
3. FAMILY — KIND-DEFINITION content (Registry-model-owned; not envelope fields)
==================================================================================================

ELEMENT     subject_model
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  one value from the closed set   W | E | P | R | V | I
              W  World       E  Epistemic   P  Production
              R  Registry    V  Visual      I  Issue
            The sovereign Record Model whose own Kind taxonomy declares the subject Kind. It
            scopes subject_kind and asserts nothing else about the model: it is not a subject of
            its own, not a MODEL-DEFINITION reference, and confers no ownership.
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value, membership of the closed set
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 068 KD-5 (exactly one owning model), RF-068-1, RF-068-4 (model
            scope semantically required; a separate representation neither mandated nor
            forbidden); RMS §2; RMS §6.1. Carrying model scope as its own element, and the element
            NAME, are 069 CHOICES.
REJECT      no value                                      (KD-5)
            two or more values — ambiguous scope         (KD-5; RF-068-1)
            a value outside the set, e.g. S "Simulation" claimed as a seventh model
                                                          (RMS §2)
            a Record identifier or a runtime object       (RF-068-5, RF-068-6)

ELEMENT     subject_kind
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  names one Kind exactly as the Kind taxonomy of the model in subject_model declares it
            — for example CHARACTER under W, ARC under P, KIND-DEFINITION under R. The name is
            read only within subject_model: the pair (subject_model, subject_kind) is the
            semantic subject. The value names the Kind itself — never a Record of that Kind,
            never a KIND-DEFINITION Record, never a two-character kind code (SC-069-C).
            Declared status. The named Kind must be a declared Kind of subject_model, with that
            status established by the owning model's own Kind architecture (068 KD-2, RF-068-1;
            Artifact 063 §8). A KIND-DEFINITION neither declares nor admits it (068 KD-2, KD-7).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence; a single value; the value is not shaped as a Record identifier
            under the universal grammar (RMS §5); the pair is not (W, WSV).
            EXTERNAL — declared status. The proof comes from the owning model's Kind
            architecture (Artifact 063 SC-063-H) and is enforced on the downstream validation
            path within those rows' own Val (rows 112, 116). This contract does not prove it,
            and an undetermined subject is not legal (Artifact 063 RB-6; 068 RF-068-1).
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 068 KD-1, KD-2, KD-5, RF-068-1 to RF-068-3; Artifact 063 §6,
            §8.3, SC-063-G (the form of a declaration reference is the family's to fix). Naming
            the Kind by its declared name is a 069 CHOICE, consistent with row 075's Val — "names
            match the RMS §10.1 roster exactly" — and with kind codes outside World being
            unfrozen (Artifact 063 §9). The element NAME is a 069 CHOICE.
REJECT      no value                                      (KD-1)               NATIVE
            two or more Kinds, e.g. CHARACTER and ORGANIZATION together
                                                          (KD-1; RF-068-1)     NATIVE
            a Record identifier, e.g. W-CH-…-Maximus      (domain instance; RF-068-2, RF-068-5)
                                                                               NATIVE
            a KIND-DEFINITION Record's identifier, R-<kind>-…
                                                          (Kind ≠ its definition; RF-068-3)
                                                                               NATIVE
            WSV under W — the WSV singleton is not a Kind (Roadmap PART III)    NATIVE
            a name the owning model has not declared — a candidate; a rejected candidate such
            as BELIEF under E; a subtype such as GENERATED-IMAGE under V
                                                          (068 §10; KD-2)      EXTERNAL
            a declared name under the wrong model, e.g. CHARACTER under P
                                                          (KD-5)               EXTERNAL

ELEMENT     definition
LAYER       FAMILY
REQUIRED    yes
CARDINALITY exactly-one
CONSTRAINT  the governed Kind-level meaning of the subject: what a Record of that Kind is — what
            holds of every Record of the Kind (068 §5; Artifact 062 L2). Non-empty. Its internal
            form is not prescribed by this contract. It carries none of: the Kind's admission
            rationale or answers to RMS §13's questions (KD-7); the owning model's taxonomy or
            the Kind's place in it (KD-4, KD-8); any Record of the Kind or its values (KD-3); the
            structural schema of the Kind's Records (KD-6); another Registry family's content
            (KD-9); the owning model's identity semantics, lifecycle, relationship packaging,
            temporal architecture, provenance or canonicality meaning, semantic validation or
            package composition (KD-10).
CHECK       NATIVE — presence, a single value, non-empty.
            EXTERNAL — the content limits are semantic and not decidable from structure; they
            are judged against 068, and this contract does not claim them proven.
BASIS       REQUIRED SYNTHESIS — 068 §5, KD-3, KD-6, KD-7, KD-9, KD-10; RMS §6.1 (governs; never
            instantiates); Blueprint §9.4 Kind semantics row. The element NAME, the single carrier
            and the non-empty rule are 069 CHOICES.
REJECT      executable behaviour, a factory, a registration, approval or admission action
                                                          (KD-3, KD-7)
            a domain instance, domain state, derived output or runtime object used as the source
            of meaning                                    (RF-068-5, RF-068-6; 062 D-3, D-5)
            the field list, requiredness or cardinality of the subject Kind's Records
                                                          (KD-6)

==================================================================================================
4. STRUCTURAL PROHIBITIONS
==================================================================================================

P-01A Artifact 069 introduces no element beyond the ten of §1. Prohibited here as universal
      semantics (P-06), as ownership, admission or sovereignty (P-03) or as runtime structure
      (068 RF-068-6): status, tier, lifecycle_state, canonical, history, relationship_record,
      owner, owns_records, admitted, admission_rationale, taxonomy_member, implementation,
      service, worker, session, process, handler, factory. Who may propose, approve or
      deprecate a definition is Artifact 065's and is not represented here.
P-01B Artifact 069 introduces no version, revision, latest-version, supersession, replacement,
      deprecation, retirement, effective-date, compatibility or retention element or mechanism.
      That representation is deferred to rows 108–110: neither defined nor permanently
      prohibited here. Whatever those rows establish stays Registry-owned, is not an envelope
      field (P-05) and is not a universal semantic shared by W, E, P, V or I (P-06).
P-02  No generic reference list (definition_refs, kind_refs, schema_refs, field_refs,
      subtype_refs, dependencies, related_records). A structural reference encodes only an
      obligation 068 establishes — here, the subject and its model scope — or representation a
      named downstream owner establishes; an admissible target category alone authorizes
      nothing (068 RF-068-4; Artifact 063 RB-5).
P-03  No element names, carries or implies ownership of the subject Kind or of its Records,
      admission or approval of the Kind, membership in a taxonomy, or sovereignty. The owning
      model keeps its taxonomy, admission, Records and domain meaning; for a Registry Kind,
      Registry holds them by its own sovereignty, not by a KIND-DEFINITION (068 KD-4).
P-04  Not the schema of any defined Kind. No element carries the fields, requiredness,
      cardinality or order of the subject Kind's Records; those are the owning model's schema
      rows, for example row 184 (068 KD-6; RULE G).
P-05  No envelope field added, removed or renamed; the family elements are not envelope fields
      (RMS §4).
P-06  None of RMS §4's prohibited universal semantics: Record base, Relationship Record,
      History Record, lifecycle, canonicality, Kind taxonomy, identity composition, state model,
      semantic schema.
P-07  Not another family's contract: not MODEL-, SUBTYPE-, FIELD-, SCHEMA- or
      RELATIONSHIP-TYPE-DEFINITION, and not CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY. No element embeds subtype,
      field, vocabulary or schema definitions (068 KD-9).
P-08  No element records the LS-1 pairing, the Kind specification artifact or a lockstep
      partner. LS-1 is authoring atomicity, not a reference (068 §16; RF-068-9).
P-09  No dependency element. The subject relation is a declaration reference, not by itself a
      semantic dependency (068 RF-068-9; Artifact 062 D-9).

==================================================================================================
5. BOUNDARIES
==================================================================================================

RESOLUTION      A conforming Record is identity-bearing (§2), so the shared resolution mechanism
                can resolve it once committed. Resolution never relies on slug, subject_model or
                subject_kind. This contract implements no resolver, lookup, index or storage,
                and does not say how a consumer finds the definition of a given Kind. Resolvable
                is not legal (Artifact 063 §11). Registry definition resolution by id+version is
                row 115's; create/resolve/version operations are row 114's. (068 RS-068-1 to
                RS-068-5)

VERSIONABILITY  Nothing here prevents the Registry evolution and versioning model of rows
                108–110 from applying to a KIND-DEFINITION. Artifact 069 defines no version
                identifier, numbering scheme, pinning representation, supersession,
                replacement or deprecation representation, retention or compatibility rule, or
                temporal lifecycle mechanism; those decisions stay with rows 108 (evolution),
                109 (versioning, pinning) and 110 (supersession, deprecation). This contract is
                open to whatever Registry-owned representation those rows establish, provided it
                leaves the seven-field envelope unchanged and keeps within the Record Model
                boundaries (P-05, P-06). Versionable therefore means: Artifact 069 does not
                structurally obstruct the evolution and versioning architecture rows 108–110 own.
                Absence here is not a decision that a KIND-DEFINITION carries no version.
                (068 §13)

REFERENCES      The subject is a declaration reference to a declared Kind of a declared Record
                Model — not an R→R reference to a KIND-DEFINITION Record, not an owned edge and
                not a Relationship Record (068 RF-068-3; Artifact 063 §8.3). No W/E/P/V/I
                domain instance, no domain state and no runtime instance is a target or an
                authority. A reference transfers no ownership, admission or authority.
                (068 RF-068-1 to RF-068-9)

LAYER           A KIND-DEFINITION sits at L2, Kind semantics (Artifact 062 §4.3). No element
                takes meaning from L3, L4 or L5, and this contract carries no dependency
                element (P-09). Whether Records of an L1 family's Kind depend on their Kind's
                KIND-DEFINITION is not established and not decided here (SC-069-J).

LS-1            This is the generic structural contract every concrete KIND-DEFINITION Record
                conforms to (row 069 Why). It is not itself an LS-1 partner of any Kind: the
                Registry's own pairs are 064 ↔ 075, and the other sets are rows 178, 257, 300,
                345 and 364. 068 ↔ 069 is not a Kind ↔ KIND-DEFINITION pair (Roadmap §0.7).

MATERIALIZATION This file is an authored source. A KIND-DEFINITION Record conforming to it is
                committed to canon/registry/** only through the Mutation Coordinator after
                G-CANON-R (Roadmap §0.8, PART X). Row 075 authors the fourteen Registry
                KIND-DEFINITIONs as canonicalization sources conforming to 069; rows 178, 257,
                300, 345 and 364 carry G: G-CANON-R. Nothing here authors or commits any of them.

DOWNSTREAM      Row 069's → names all Kind schemas, 074 and 075. A domain Kind schema conforms
                to its Kind's KIND-DEFINITION — row 186: "conforms to its KIND-DEFINITION and to
                the World field definitions" — not to this file; this contract imposes no
                structure on any domain Kind schema (SC-069-K). Row 074 specifies the Registry
                self-definition set; row 075 authors it. Neither is pre-built here.

==================================================================================================
6. DECISION CASES (schematic — no identifier is minted; nothing here is Registry data)
==================================================================================================

ACCEPT    subject_model W, subject_kind CHARACTER, definition carrying the governed meaning of
          CHARACTER — World keeps CHARACTER and every Character Record              NATIVE
                                                     + EXTERNAL (declared status: World's)
ACCEPT    subject_model P, subject_kind ARC — same family, a separate taxonomy        NATIVE
                                                     + EXTERNAL (declared status: Production's)
ACCEPT    subject_model R, subject_kind KIND-DEFINITION, envelope kind KIND-DEFINITION — the
          Record defining the Kind KIND-DEFINITION, one of row 075's fourteen; the two values
          coincide in two different roles; no axiom Record, no regress (RMS §10.4)  NATIVE
                                                     + EXTERNAL (declared status: RMS §10.1; 064)
BOUNDARY  one subject in two carriers, subject_model and subject_kind — conforming; this is the
          contract's own shape (§1)                                                  STATIC
BOUNDARY  every NATIVE check passes but the Kind's declared status cannot be established — not
          legal (Artifact 063 RB-6)                                                  EXTERNAL
BOUNDARY  structurally conforming, not yet resolved by any consumer — the structure conforms;
          whether it resolves is row 115's, and resolvable is not legal              EXTERNAL
BOUNDARY  a version element present today — not defined by this contract; its representation
          is 108–110's to establish (P-01B)                                          STATIC
REJECT    subject_kind absent, or subject_model absent                              NATIVE
REJECT    subject_kind CHARACTER and ORGANIZATION together                          NATIVE
REJECT    subject_model W and E together — ambiguous scope                          NATIVE
REJECT    subject_model S, claimed as a seventh sovereign Record Model               NATIVE
REJECT    subject_kind W-CH-…-Maximus — a World domain instance                      NATIVE
REJECT    subject_kind R-<kind>-… — a KIND-DEFINITION Record, not a Kind             NATIVE
REJECT    subject_model W, subject_kind WSV — the WSV singleton is not a Kind         NATIVE
REJECT    subject_model E, subject_kind BELIEF — rejected candidate, not declared     EXTERNAL
REJECT    subject_model V, subject_kind GENERATED-IMAGE — a subtype, not a Kind      EXTERNAL
REJECT    subject_model P, subject_kind CHARACTER — not declared by Production       EXTERNAL
REJECT    definition citing W-CH-…-Maximus as what a Character is                    EXTERNAL
REJECT    kind given as an invented code such as KD                                  NATIVE

