7. SOURCE CONDITIONS
==================================================================================================

SC-069-A  LS-1. Row 069 carries LS: LS-1 and Why: LS-1 — the schema every concrete
          KIND-DEFINITION Record conforms to. Read through that Why and Roadmap §0.7 (rows 068
          and 069 distinguish the generic family and schema from the concrete sets), 069 is not
          the partner of any one Kind. The Registry's own pairs stay 064 ↔ 075
          (AD-LS1-R-BOOTSTRAP). Recorded; nothing to resolve here.
SC-069-B  No schema language is established. The notation of §0 is Artifact 067's local choice,
          reused, with CHECK added as a 069 choice; it is no repository-wide language.
SC-069-C  No two-character Registry Kind code is established, and kind codes outside World are
          not frozen (Artifact 063 §9). The envelope kind is constrained symbolically, and the
          subject Kind is named, not coded. Identity binding is row 117's.
SC-069-D  Req: RR-16 is carried exactly; its text is unavailable (GAP-C) and is not invented.
SC-069-E  Row 069 carries T: schema · Canon: canonical-about-meaning · CD: yes on a docs/** path.
          Artifact 003's general convention gives a docs/** specification Canon: n/a; whether it
          reaches a schema contract is not stated. The metadata is preserved exactly; this file
          is not a Registry Record, and CD: yes licenses nothing (068 SC-068-G; SC-067-H).
          Recorded, not resolved.
SC-069-F  Declared status has no single proof mechanism across the six models (Artifact 063
          SC-063-H). subject_kind's declared status is therefore an EXTERNAL check whose proof
          is the owning model's; this contract does not prove it and does not define how it is
          proved. Recorded, not resolved; non-blocking.
SC-069-G  VERDICT. Row 399, the VERDICT Kind-Definition, carries H: 069,398 and is ordered
          before row 405, which admits VERDICT (068 SC-068-J; CONFLICT-A). A Record with
          subject_model P and subject_kind VERDICT passes the NATIVE checks and fails the
          EXTERNAL declared-status check while VERDICT is provisional. Recorded; non-blocking.
SC-069-H  If a model's Kind specification and its KIND-DEFINITION diverge, which side yields is
          not established (068 SC-068-K). This contract carries no precedence element.
          Recorded; non-blocking.
SC-069-I  What happens to a retired Kind's KIND-DEFINITION is not established (068 SC-068-M).
          This contract carries no retirement or deprecation element (P-01B). Recorded.
SC-069-J  Whether Records of an L1 family's Kind depend on their Kind's KIND-DEFINITION is not
          established (068 SC-068-L). This contract carries no dependency element and invents no
          exemption from Artifact 062 D-8. Recorded; routed to rows 074 and 111.
SC-069-K  Row 069's → names all Kind schemas, but domain Kind schemas list their own H (for
          example row 186: H: 185,182) and conform to their Kind's KIND-DEFINITION, not to this
          file. The unlock is read as row 069's own metadata; this contract imposes nothing on
          those schemas beyond their rows. Recorded; non-blocking.

